<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ══ JOY BRUSH's own tokens ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  D.01. One file, one place to change a colour.

  Joy Brush is its own Gradle module, so it cannot @color-reference the app's tokens: a
  library's resources cannot see the consuming app's resources. Every token here is
  therefore one of exactly three things, and tools/check_joybrush_tokens.py enforces that
  there is no fourth.

    1. THE ROOM PAIR · jb_room_start and jb_room_end, the only two lines in this file that
       nobody mirrors. The OWNER edits those two lines and nothing else, and the change
       ripples into the room gradient, the Canvas board gradient and everything drawn with
       them. Six-digit hex, so opaque; #AARRGGBB would read the same.

    2. A @color/ REFERENCE to a token in this same file (the Canvas board, which must
       always equal the room, and the character board, which must always equal the puppet
       board). Nothing to drift.

    3. A MIRROR of a token in app/src/main/res/values/studio_tokens.xml, carrying a
       trailing comment of the form  mirror: s_token  that names its source. One token
       takes its source from Studio.java instead and reads  mirror: Studio.SUNK, because
       that colour has no XML twin.

  Why the owner may change the room pair but not the mirrors: the mirrors are the
  ecosystem. State colours (cyan = selected, pink = live, amber = careful, red = destroys)
  are global and constant, so they are mirrors and must stay mirrors. INBOX.md, 2026-09-12:
  "STATE colours are global and constant ... A section accent must never be a colour that
  already means a state."

  ══ DO NOT REINTRODUCE A PINK-RED → AMBER/ORANGE ROOM GRADIENT ══════════════════════
  The owner's own first idea for the Joy Brush gradient was a pink-red → yellow/orange
  pair. It is rejected here on purpose, and this note exists so it is not reintroduced by
  accident: it starts on the red family, which already MEANS "something is being
  destroyed", and it ends on amber, which already MEANS "careful, or unsaved". A room
  gradient that wears two state colours stops being an identity. The placeholder below is
  "Ink", indigo → bright blue: 25 degrees from SELECTED cyan, and nowhere near LIVE,
  CAREFUL or DANGER (JOYBRUSH_VISUAL_LANGUAGE.md §4.2). Changing it is the owner's call.
  Changing it without a decision is not.
  ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-->
<resources>

    <!-- ══ IDENTITY ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         The two lines the owner owns. Everything else in this file mirrors. -->
    <color name="jb_room_start">#5C43FD</color>   <!-- indigo; the owner may change this line -->
    <color name="jb_room_end">#4397FD</color>     <!-- bright blue; the owner may change this line -->

    <!-- ══ BOARDS ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         "Boards wear the colours of what they connect to" (owner, 2026-09-28). A board's
         identity is a FILL with its type glyph punched out of it; a coloured RING already
         means a state. Its edge stays neutral, jb_line.
         Canvas is Joy Brush itself, so it IS the room pair, by reference. -->
    <color name="jb_board_canvas_start">@color/jb_room_start</color>
    <color name="jb_board_canvas_end">@color/jb_room_end</color>

    <!-- Animation feeds the Studio as video, and video wears the Studio room. -->
    <color name="jb_board_animation_start">#FF35F6BF</color>   <!-- mirror: s_room_studio -->
    <color name="jb_board_animation_end">#FF97FE8B</color>     <!-- mirror: s_go_end -->

    <!-- Sprite feeds SpriteLab: neon pink → vivid purple. -->
    <color name="jb_board_sprite_start">#FFFF008C</color>      <!-- mirror: s_room_sprite -->
    <color name="jb_board_sprite_end">#FFCC27FF</color>        <!-- mirror: s_room_avatar -->

    <!-- Puppet and Character both feed Avatar Studio: vivid purple → purple. -->
    <color name="jb_board_puppet_start">#FFCC27FF</color>      <!-- mirror: s_room_avatar -->
    <color name="jb_board_puppet_end">#FF8C3DFA</color>        <!-- mirror: s_room_avatar_deep -->
    <color name="jb_board_character_start">@color/jb_board_puppet_start</color>
    <color name="jb_board_character_end">@color/jb_board_puppet_end</color>

    <!-- ══ STATE ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         Global and constant. Always a ring, never a fill, except jb_state_destroy: red
         fills are the one exception in the whole app, and only for something being lost. -->
    <color name="jb_state_selected">#FF22D3EE</color>          <!-- mirror: s_armed -->
    <color name="jb_state_live">#FFF43F8E</color>              <!-- mirror: s_live -->
    <color name="jb_state_careful">#FFFBBF24</color>           <!-- mirror: s_careful -->
    <color name="jb_state_destroy">#FFFA3D5D</color>           <!-- mirror: s_danger -->

    <!-- ══ SURFACES ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         The ground ramp, named by meaning, so a Joy Brush screen never needs a fifth. -->
    <color name="jb_ground">#FF000000</color>                  <!-- mirror: s_ground -->
    <color name="jb_surface">#FF0D0D10</color>                 <!-- mirror: s_surface -->
    <color name="jb_panel">#FF111114</color>                   <!-- mirror: s_panel -->
    <color name="jb_sunk">#FF16161B</color>                    <!-- mirror: Studio.SUNK -->
    <color name="jb_raised">#FF1C1C22</color>                  <!-- mirror: s_raised -->
    <color name="jb_line">#FF2C2C35</color>                    <!-- mirror: s_line -->

    <!-- ══ INK, SOLID ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         Text on ordinary surfaces. -->
    <color name="jb_ink">#FFE4E4E7</color>                     <!-- mirror: s_ink -->
    <color name="jb_ink_dim">#FFA1A1AA</color>                 <!-- mirror: s_ink_dim -->
    <color name="jb_ink_faint">#FF71717A</color>               <!-- mirror: s_ink_faint -->
    <color name="jb_ink_off">#FF4B4B55</color>                 <!-- mirror: s_ink_off -->
    <color name="jb_label">#FFC4C4CE</color>                   <!-- mirror: s_label -->

    <!-- ══ INK, OVER THE PICTURE ════════════════════════════════════════════════
         The frosted-drawer ramp, raised so text survives a blown-out frame. Nothing
         outside a drawer or popover may use these. -->
    <color name="jb_drawer_ink">#FFF2F2F5</color>              <!-- mirror: s_drawer_ink -->
    <color name="jb_drawer_dim">#FFC9C9D3</color>              <!-- mirror: s_drawer_dim -->
    <color name="jb_drawer_label">#FFC4C4CE</color>            <!-- mirror: s_drawer_label -->
</resources>
